        "pf": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Benefits you'll feel",
            "key": "feel",
            "heading": "What people\nnotice first",
            "lede": "What customers tell us they notice first. Individual experiences, not a promise. Open any of them for more.",
            "image_fallback": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0976/2724/2843/files/nad-benefits-feel.jpg?v=1791019769",
            "image_alt": "A cyclist pausing mid-ride in the sun, sunglasses pushed up, catching their breath",
            "image_position": "50% 8%",
            "cta_label": "Start your 90 days",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "f1": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "panel": "feel",
            "title": "Energy that doesn't spike",
            "sub": "“No afternoon slump and in general feeling great” – Lynda",
            "text": "<p>NAD+ sits at the centre of how your cells turn food into usable energy. Topping up the pathway supports a steadier supply rather than the peak-and-crash of a stimulant, which is why most people notice it in the afternoon rather than the first hour.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f2": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "panel": "feel",
            "title": "Recovery between sessions",
            "sub": "“Has actually changed my recovery” – Adam H",
            "text": "<p>Recovery is where ageing tends to show up first: the session is fine, the next day isn't. Customers most often report the gap between hard days closing before anything moves in their data.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f3": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "panel": "feel",
            "title": "Steadier mornings",
            "sub": "“I predominantly struggle with mornings but already feel myself finding these easier” – Becca",
            "text": "<p>The first hour is the one you can judge without a device. A clearer start, on the same sleep, is the earliest signal most people report.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f4": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "panel": "feel",
            "title": "A calmer baseline",
            "sub": "“Energy is up and staying consistent” – Jack",
            "text": "<p>Not a lift, a floor. The change people describe is less in how high the good days go and more in how far the bad ones drop.</p>"
          }
        },
        "pt": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Ways to check",
            "key": "track",
            "heading": "Three ways\nto check it",
            "lede": "Use whichever suits you, or all three. Compare against your own starting point at day 30, 60 and 90.",
            "image_fallback": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0976/2724/2843/files/nad-benefits-track.jpg?v=1791020038",
            "image_alt": "A runner sitting on a log after a session, checking the watch on their wrist",
            "image_position": "",
            "cta_label": "Start your 90 days",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "ck1": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "panel": "track",
            "title": "A weekly how-I-feel check-in",
            "sub": "30 seconds, no device needed",
            "text": "<p>Once a week, rate your energy, sleep, afternoons and mood out of 10. Felt changes are easy to forget, so writing them down turns a feeling into a record you can look back on.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ck2": {
          "type": "benefit",
